From 3ed1dfb51035340f61e319482222d19fdbc91f94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:44:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(differential): run the native adapter against a stand-in
 backend

Codecov reported 30 uncovered lines on this branch, all in
`src/analysis/differential.jl`: the adapter that turns a CompositionalDA
result into result rows. CompositionalDA is not in the General registry, so
CI cannot install it, and only the refusal path ran.

- `differential_abundance(...; native_backend=nothing)` calls a module. The
  default is the `CompositionalDA` this session loaded, or the by-name refusal
  when it loaded none. Production behaviour is unchanged.
- `_is_composition_error` translates the `CompositionError` of the backend in
  use.
- `diagnostics.native_method.package` reports the name of the module that
  produced the numbers, so a stand-in record cannot read as a package record.

`test/support/native_da_stub.jl` has the two entry points, the column names
and the verdict strings of the package. Its `qvalue` is not
`bh_adjust(pvalue)`, so a second BH pass is visible, and its structural rows
carry NaN as the package leaves them.

`test/unit/test_differential_native.jl` gains four testsets that run on every
checkout: the seam, the ALDEx2 wiring, the ANCOM-BC wiring and the refusal
order. The comparisons against the real package stay, and still skip with a
message when the package is absent.

Measured with Julia 1.12.5, `--code-coverage=user --compiled-modules=no`,
`test/runtests.jl differential differential_native`: 1159 pass, 13 skipped;
every instrumented line this branch adds to `differential.jl` is covered
(52 of 52).

